\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Synthetic kinetic-trap benchmark ($N=2{,}000$, $T=1{,}000$), initialized in Basin A. Dashed circles mark basin cores ($r^2<0.45$); the gold contour marks $V=-1.2\text  { kcal/mol}$. (a)~Brownian dynamics diffuses without drift. (b)~Standard Langevin concentrates more terminal mass in the basin cores. (c)~Rotor-only dynamics lacks contractive restoration. (d)~A-Block combines the rotor and dilator; it has the lowest selected-mask FES RMSE and the highest transition count among the tested methods, but these finite-time metrics do not establish equilibrium accuracy.}}{4}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:kinetic_trap_benchmark}{{1}{4}{}{figure.1}{}}
