\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Finite-horizon navigation benchmark on the non-convex letterform \textit  {`G'} ($N=1{,}200$, $T=4{,}000$, identical noise amplitude $0.85$ and circular aperture boundary $r_{\text  {dish}}$ across all methods). (a)~\textbf  {Brownian Dynamics ($\mathbf  {f}=\mathbf  {0}$)}: visitation $99.3\%$, terminal coverage $90.5\%$, and precision $26.1\%$. (b)~\textbf  {Standard Langevin ($\sigma =0, \kappa =1.0$)}: precision $98.9\%$, visitation $33.2\%$, and terminal coverage $33.7\%$. (c)~\textbf  {Rotor-Only ($\sigma =11.0, \kappa =0$)}: visitation $100.0\%$, precision $0.1\%$, and terminal coverage $1.4\%$. (d)~\textbf  {Full Clifford A-Block ($\sigma =11.0, \kappa =1.8$)}: precision $99.9\%$, visitation $97.8\%$, and terminal coverage $99.2\%$. These metrics describe this finite-horizon synthetic-potential experiment and do not establish equilibrium sampling or a general navigation guarantee.}}{6}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:typography_benchmark}{{3}{6}{}{figure.3}{}}
